#!/bin/sh
# Runs on the device after opkg unpacks this package (see piko's
# tools/make-ipk.sh --postinst and libopkg/opkg_configure.c, which execs
# control/postinst itself -- nothing else invokes this).
#
# Nudges matchbox-desktop to notice gmenunx.desktop. Usually unnecessary --
# it watches the application directories with inotify and reloads on its
# own -- but that watch on a card's applications directory is only
# (re)armed when the mount table changes, so a package that is the first
# to ever create that directory on a given card (nothing existed there yet
# when the card was mounted) is missed until something asks for a rescan
# by hand. See piko's usr/sbin/deskscan for the full explanation.
#
# Swallow deskscan's exit status: it returns 1 when matchbox-desktop isn't
# running at all (e.g. installing with no graphical session up, or the
# qemu-arm offline-root test harness), which is a normal outcome here, not
# an install failure -- opkg treats a nonzero postinst as "unpacked only,
# configuration required," which would misreport a successful install.
[ -x /usr/sbin/deskscan ] && /usr/sbin/deskscan
exit 0
